Passage: DIR, Annex I, 2.1.1

[0] 2.1.1.
[1] General Machinery intended for use with foodstuffs or with cosmetics or pharmaceutical products must be designed and constructed in such a way as to avoid any risk of infection, sickness or contagion.
[2] The following requirements must be observed:
[3] (a) materials in contact with, or intended to come into contact with, foodstuffs or cosmetics or pharmaceutical products must satisfy the conditions set down in the relevant Directives.
[4] The machinery must be designed and constructed in such a way that these materials can be cleaned before each use.
[5] Where this is not possible disposable parts must be used;
[6] (b) all surfaces in contact with foodstuffs or cosmetics or pharmaceutical products, other than surfaces of disposable parts, must: — be smooth and have neither ridges nor crevices which could harbour organic materials.
[7] The same applies to their joinings, — be designed and constructed in such a way as to reduce the projections, edges and recesses of assemblies to a minimum, — be easily cleaned and disinfected, where necessary after removing easily dismantled parts;
[8] the inside surfaces must have curves with a radius sufficient to allow thorough cleaning;
[9] (c) it must be possible for liquids, gases and aerosols deriving from foodstuffs, cosmetics or pharmaceutical products as well as from cleaning, disinfecting and rinsing fluids to be completely discharged from the machinery (if possible, in a ‘cleaning’ position);
[10] (d) machinery must be designed and constructed in such a way as to prevent any substances or living creatures, in particular insects, from entering, or any organic matter from accumulating in, areas that cannot be cleaned;
[11] (e) machinery must be designed and constructed in such a way that no ancillary substances hazardous to health, including the lubricants used, can come into contact with foodstuffs, cosmetics or pharmaceutical products.
[12] Where necessary, machinery must be designed and constructed in such a way that continuing compliance with this requirement can be checked.
